DE operating standard. Full text: "Token discipline" section of `AGENTS.md`. Repo-specific rules and Completion Program lanes/stop gates take precedence.

- One slice = one fresh session, started from the latest DE handoff block, not old chat history.
- Before significant coding, declare: objective, likely files, acceptance criteria, verification commands, boundaries.
- Search before reading. Open only files the slice needs; read ranges of large files. No whole-repo reads without reason. Don't reopen unchanged files.
- Two-failure stop: after two materially failed attempts at the same issue, stop and write a checkpoint (behavior, attempts + why failed, evidence, suspected root cause, next investigation). No speculative patch loops.
- Economy models for mechanical work (inventory, repetitive edits, refactors, docs, lint, simple tests). Premium only for architecture, security, identity/auth, billing/payment, migrations, hard debugging, cross-repo contracts, high-risk final review.
- Targeted tests while iterating; full suite once before checkpoint. Trim tool output.
- End with the DE handoff block; record limit hits, model used, manual rescues under USAGE SIGNALS.
